Null pointer = a pointer that is pointing to zero address (address 0).

cint *ip = NULL;      // NULL pointer
*ip = 35;            // WRITE (NULL pointer dereference → WRITE error)

If we are trying to update any data using null pointer → will get runtime error.
If we perform any operation on null pointer → will get runtime error.
Zero/null address is a special address that the compiler uses to do some special tasks.

cint *ip;
ip = (int *)0;    // null pointer
*ip = 35;         // WRITE → RTE
